WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.319 --> 00:00:02.236
- Okay, we're in Vegas.

00:00:03.578 --> 00:00:05.032
It's morning in Vegas, which means

00:00:05.032 --> 00:00:07.615
we partied too hard last night.

00:00:08.702 --> 00:00:11.135
I don't know who's the most hungover.

00:00:11.135 --> 00:00:13.522
- I'd say probably me, I'm feeling--

00:00:13.522 --> 00:00:14.661
- I went to bed at 10pm.

00:00:14.661 --> 00:00:17.173
- 10pm, you went to bed at 10pm in Vegas.

00:00:17.173 --> 00:00:18.423
- That's right.

00:00:19.826 --> 00:00:21.780
- So before we came to
Vegas I sent out a tweet,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.647
asking where we should get hangover food.

00:00:23.647 --> 00:00:26.270
One place sort of stood out,
that people recommended.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.292
It's called KoMex, so we're
on our way now to KoMex.

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:30.125
- [Steven] KoMex.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:33.905
- We're gonna see just how
good Korean and Mexican food

00:00:33.905 --> 00:00:35.905
are curing our hangover.

00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:41.846
(soft music)

00:00:41.846 --> 00:00:45.472
- I'm gonna give you a nice loud clap.

00:00:45.472 --> 00:00:47.404
- I feel like one thing that's
nice when you're hungover

00:00:47.404 --> 00:00:49.897
is to just lean against a nice brick wall.

00:00:49.897 --> 00:00:50.814
- Is that real brick?

00:00:50.814 --> 00:00:52.856
- I can't tell.

00:00:52.856 --> 00:00:54.256
- [Keith] It's just a perspective trick.

00:00:54.256 --> 00:00:56.359
- [Shane] It's not real, it's not real.

00:00:56.359 --> 00:00:57.192
- It's not real.

00:00:57.192 --> 00:00:58.864
- Sorry you're having
such a rough morning.

00:00:58.864 --> 00:01:00.552
- What's the history of KoMex?

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:02.431
- Well we actually owned a Mexican market

00:01:02.431 --> 00:01:03.473
for over 20 years.

00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:06.370
We would bring home
bulgogi meats, all of that

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.069
and my husband would just actually take

00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:09.415
the pico de gallo he had, a tortilla,

00:01:09.415 --> 00:01:11.719
just kind of wrap it up and
eat it with Mexican rice,

00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:13.282
whatever we had at the market.

00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:14.437
- That's awesome.

00:01:14.437 --> 00:01:16.888
We want to eat everything.

00:01:16.888 --> 00:01:20.590
It's got fries and it's got chippies.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.757
Whoa, baby go.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:26.106
It tastes like Korean barbecue

00:01:26.106 --> 00:01:27.665
and it tastes like french fries.

00:01:27.665 --> 00:01:29.738
- It's fun to be messy
when you're hungover,

00:01:29.738 --> 00:01:31.481
have like there's messy meal.

00:01:31.481 --> 00:01:33.258
- Jalapenos are nice and spicy.

00:01:33.258 --> 00:01:35.091
Wake yourself up baby.

00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:37.237
- Yeah, man.

00:01:37.237 --> 00:01:39.134
- They know how to fix this thing.

00:01:39.134 --> 00:01:41.031
- Put your energy down.

00:01:41.031 --> 00:01:41.864
- Why?

00:01:41.864 --> 00:01:42.697
- Please.

00:01:42.697 --> 00:01:43.530
- I'm happy.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.605
- [Brian] Because we're
hangover and you're yelling.

00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:46.247
- I can't do with this volume right now.

00:01:46.247 --> 00:01:50.250
- The spice opens up my
hungover closed sinuses.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.551
- I want to say it's like if Taco Bell

00:01:51.551 --> 00:01:53.294
were very, very, very good.

00:01:53.294 --> 00:01:54.791
'Cause you know how
Taco Bell's always like,

00:01:54.791 --> 00:01:56.753
well what if it's a pizza.

00:01:56.753 --> 00:01:57.753
- Holy moly.

00:01:58.991 --> 00:02:00.938
What's better than nachos and fries?

00:02:00.938 --> 00:02:02.470
Tater tot, that's what's better.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.370
And I can't believe that
they understand that

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.190
and that they serve this as a meal.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:09.773
The tater tops are
golden, they're perfect.

00:02:10.965 --> 00:02:11.798
- You're a little baby.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.316
- You're bullying me,
I'm not a little baby.

00:02:13.316 --> 00:02:14.198
- [Steven] Little baby.

00:02:14.198 --> 00:02:15.031
- [Keith] Steven, you're not going to

00:02:15.031 --> 00:02:17.114
be able to eat that bite.

00:02:19.192 --> 00:02:20.025
- [Shane] Hold it in your mouth.

00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:22.743
- That's not how anyone
wants anyone else to eat.

00:02:22.743 --> 00:02:26.710
It felt like my cheeks just
started sagging to the floor.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.931
'Cause they're filled
with such delicious meat.

00:02:28.931 --> 00:02:30.177
- There's nothing I like more

00:02:30.177 --> 00:02:33.101
than stuffing my face with tater tots.

00:02:33.101 --> 00:02:36.778
- I can't look at your face
while you speak to me anymore.

00:02:36.778 --> 00:02:38.676
- Bulgogi chimichanga.

00:02:38.676 --> 00:02:41.785
So, it looks like a Mexican chimichange

00:02:41.785 --> 00:02:44.260
but instead it actually
has bulgogi meat in there.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.293
- [Keith] This sauce smells so good.

00:02:46.293 --> 00:02:48.691
- I feel like this isn't gonna
be too bad on my stomach.

00:02:48.691 --> 00:02:49.942
It is somehow light.

00:02:49.942 --> 00:02:51.244
- I don't feel light at all right now.

00:02:51.244 --> 00:02:53.222
- I feel light, I feel light as a feather.

00:02:53.222 --> 00:02:56.291
- This is what hangover food is about.

00:02:56.291 --> 00:02:57.939
It looks beautiful when it arrives

00:02:57.939 --> 00:03:00.216
and immediately a disaster on your plate

00:03:00.216 --> 00:03:04.065
but like a disaster that you
want to lick up every drop of.

00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:08.232
- Hangover food should
become a beautiful disaster

00:03:09.514 --> 00:03:11.554
like your night prior.

00:03:11.554 --> 00:03:12.387
- Oh yeah.

00:03:14.755 --> 00:03:17.077
- This is kind of like
one, just big jumbo.

00:03:17.077 --> 00:03:18.147
It's one flavor.

00:03:18.147 --> 00:03:20.902
- This is more uniform whereas
the other one was like,

00:03:20.902 --> 00:03:22.316
hey, have a little bit of this.

00:03:22.316 --> 00:03:23.864
Uh, where's this crunch coming from?

00:03:23.864 --> 00:03:25.443
- I am waking up, certainly.

00:03:25.443 --> 00:03:26.948
I feel like a lot better.

00:03:26.948 --> 00:03:30.081
I'm starting to feel better.

00:03:30.081 --> 00:03:31.035
I'm stretching.

00:03:31.035 --> 00:03:32.853
- [Lynda] So this is the last item.

00:03:32.853 --> 00:03:34.785
Koreans, after a drunken night out,

00:03:34.785 --> 00:03:36.545
want something spicy and so

00:03:36.545 --> 00:03:38.727
this is a kimchi chicken fried rice.

00:03:38.727 --> 00:03:40.664
- Can I pop the the yolk?

00:03:40.664 --> 00:03:42.914
- You can pop the yolk, bro

00:03:44.284 --> 00:03:45.792
- You did that so--

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.155
Why did you do it like that?

00:03:47.155 --> 00:03:48.308
- I'm sorry.

00:03:48.308 --> 00:03:50.155
- I actually normally don't eat kimchi

00:03:50.155 --> 00:03:51.844
because I know that kimchi's spicy

00:03:51.844 --> 00:03:53.398
and normally when I'm about to eat it

00:03:53.398 --> 00:03:57.565
one of my friend says, "No,
Keith, don't eat this."

00:03:58.436 --> 00:03:59.457
It's like acidic spicy.

00:03:59.457 --> 00:04:02.051
- Sometimes spice is a great
way to wake yourself up.

00:04:02.051 --> 00:04:02.884
- [Keith] That's true.

00:04:02.884 --> 00:04:06.670
- And this kimchi is just
clearing up my sinuses,

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.593
opening up my eyes and
getting me ready for the day.

00:04:09.593 --> 00:04:12.001
- At Korean barbecue places a lot of times

00:04:12.001 --> 00:04:13.731
they'll finish grilling everything

00:04:13.731 --> 00:04:15.832
and then when they're done
they'll take all that grease.

00:04:15.832 --> 00:04:16.858
- Oh, man.

00:04:16.858 --> 00:04:18.703
- And make kimchi fried rice.

00:04:18.703 --> 00:04:19.923
Oh, it's so good.

00:04:19.923 --> 00:04:22.386
- This is just belly cement basically.

00:04:22.386 --> 00:04:24.034
Really tasty belly cement.

00:04:24.034 --> 00:04:26.055
- I just love rice, you know.

00:04:26.055 --> 00:04:29.853
Fried rice, white rice,
steamed rice, sticky rice.

00:04:29.853 --> 00:04:32.471
- Uh, I'm beginning to get a little sweat.

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:34.970
I'm gonna start to glisten,
I'm gonna start to glisten.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.204
So how's my hangover now
as compared to earlier?

00:04:37.204 --> 00:04:38.728
I do feel better than earlier.

00:04:38.728 --> 00:04:41.478
More energetic and ready to poop.

00:04:42.544 --> 00:04:44.366
- My hangover now has definitely improved.

00:04:44.366 --> 00:04:46.308
- You kinda looked like
hell a couple hours ago.

00:04:46.308 --> 00:04:49.119
- I felt like hell but
now I feel like a person.

00:04:49.119 --> 00:04:49.954
Thank you KoMex.

00:04:49.954 --> 00:04:53.385
- Coming out of a hangover is
one of the great joys in life.

00:04:53.385 --> 00:04:56.270
- As a totally sober person
I really enjoyed that meal

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.502
but I feel like I went in
reverse of what you guys are.

00:04:58.502 --> 00:05:01.516
'Cause I started off
this morning very awake

00:05:01.516 --> 00:05:05.933
and now I'm at that like
food baby coma moment.

00:05:05.933 --> 00:05:06.878
Cheers.

00:05:06.878 --> 00:05:07.792
- [Shane] Feeling good.

00:05:07.792 --> 00:05:09.709
- [Keith] Feeling good.

00:05:11.357 --> 00:05:14.440
(happy jingly music)

